imagine_unperceived	one
frame_ideas_omit	one
perceive_while	one
conceive_mind_indep	one
conceive_unconceived	two	unconceived	A1 C1	representing the objects in thought as existing with no one conceiving them	the objects being unconceived at the very time one conceives them
repugnant	one
# conceive_unconceived: P3 needs only the content reading. Imagining something as unperceived is enough for conceiving it possible that it exists without the mind.
# The "manifest repugnancy" behind A1 and C1 holds only on the act reading: conceiving something while it is not conceived. On the content reading there is no contradiction.
# I took repugnant as one sense, since P4 and A1 both use the act reading. The shift itself sits in conceive_unconceived.
